# Faust ESP32 Field Speaker Skill (`.claude/skills/esp32-speaker`)

### 1. Architecture & DRY Primacy
- **Shared Resident Daemon**: Reuses the Kokoro-82M neural TTS daemon on `http://127.0.0.1:20129` (RAM-pinned weights, 0ms cold-start) with Vietnamese G2P phoneme support and neural style blending.
- **Synthesizer Bridge (`/synthesize`)**: Synthesizes speech and performs high-speed polyphase sinc resampling (24kHz to 16kHz) without disk I/O.
- **Hardware UART Streamer**: Paces 16-bit mono/stereo PCM chunks across `COM5` (or configured port) at `921,600` baud with ~0.15s buffer lead.
- **Reusable C++ Package**: `packages/ui/audio/I2SSpeaker/` provides zero-pop I2S DMA playback and mono-to-stereo expansion.
- **Standalone Sketch**: `Nháp/esp32_i2s_speaker.ino` connects ESP32 to MAX98357A / I2S DAC (BCLK=GPIO16, LRC=GPIO17, DIN=GPIO15).

### 2. Commands & Usage
```bash
# Speak via ESP32 speaker
python .claude/skills/esp32-speaker/scripts/cli.py speak "<text>"

# Diagnostic test
python .claude/skills/esp32-speaker/scripts/cli.py test
```

**Why:** Grants Faust a physical speaker voice presence on embedded ESP32 actuators while reusing the exact same acoustic neural engine as the PC speaker.
**How to apply:** Link with `[[faust-resident-audio-daemon]]`, `[[faust-acoustic-engine]]`, and `[[vgwd025k3-codex-of-time]]`.
